# .mailmap — one person, one name, in every git report.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Everyone here has committed under more than one identity:
# a laptop with a different git config, a GitHub web edit using a noreply address,
# a name typed differently on a second machine. Git treats each combination as a
# separate human, so `git shortlog`, `git log --author`, and GitHub's contributor
# view all split one person's work several ways.
#
# This file fixes the DISPLAY only. It rewrites nothing, changes no commit, and is
# safe to add at any time — git just reads it when it prints an author.
#
# FORMAT:  Proper Name <proper@email>  Committed Name <committed@email>
# The right-hand pair is what is recorded in a commit; the left is what to show.
#
# Adding yourself: add a line, do not edit history. If you are about to commit from
# a new machine, `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` first — that is
# cheaper than a line here.

