# ── Derrilon Young ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Her git `user.name` was accidentally set to a whole shell command — two commands
# pasted as one — so every commit she has made is authored by a name containing
# `git config --global user.email ...`. This maps it back to her name.
#
# The address stays as the one she actually committed with rather than the one she
# meant to set, because that is the true record; changing it here would only make
# the mapping wrong in a new way. She should fix her local config so future commits
# do not need this line:
#   git config --global user.name "Derrilon Young"
#   git config --global user.email "ddy006@latech.edu"
# and once she does, add the new address to this block.
Derrilon Young <derrilondoriea@gmail.com> <derrilondoriea@gmail.com>
